# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets and machine-specific state. Everything here is generated by the
# bring-up and is specific to one machine and one run, so it is never committed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Minted emulated IAM key. aws/credentials.example is the committed template and
# scripts/01-bootstrap-iam.sh copies it into place on a fresh clone.
aws/credentials

# Kubeconfig for the two clusters: holds cluster CAs and an exec-credential block.
kubeconfig

# The lab CA and leaf certificates. Terraform regenerates these per clone, and
# the CA private key lives in the state file below -- do not publish either.
certs/*
!certs/.gitkeep

# Any other key material that happens to land in the tree (client certs,
# keystores, Evaluate-STIG signing keys).
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
*.key
*.jks

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Terraform
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.terraform/
.terraform.lock.hcl
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfvars
*.tfvars.json
crash.log
crash.*.log

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Floci's persisted emulated-AWS state. Thousands of JSON files, plus the
# write-ahead logs; recreated by `make up`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/*
!data/.gitkeep

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DISA STIG content. Not ours to redistribute, and the compilation alone is
# ~375 MB -- past GitHub's 100 MB per-file limit. Fetch it with
# `make stig-library`, which resolves the current filename itself.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
stigs/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logs and editor noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
boot.log
*.log
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# Local Claude Code configuration and skills — not part of the project.
.claude/
